#: ../../user_manual/ekos-tilt-correction.rst:208
msgid "Star detection settings for tilted setups"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/ekos-tilt-correction.rst:210
msgid ""
"The default focus star-extraction profile (``1-Focus-Default``) is tuned for "
"normal autofocus. With noticeable tilt it can starve the outer tiles of data:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/ekos-tilt-correction.rst:213
msgid ""
"It keeps only the **100 brightest stars for the whole frame**. A bright "
"cluster in the centre can use up most of that budget, leaving few stars for "
"the corner tiles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/ekos-tilt-correction.rst:215
msgid ""
"It rejects stars that are **more elongated than 1.5** (ratio a/b). The "
"slightly defocused or tilted stars in the corners are exactly the ones that "
"get dropped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/ekos-tilt-correction.rst:218
msgid ""
"Typical symptoms are corner tiles with few or no stars during the sweep, "
"bumpy per-tile V-curves, and tiles that fail to fit (N/A) even though the "
"overall autofocus solves cleanly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/ekos-tilt-correction.rst:221
msgid ""
"To fix this, create a dedicated profile for Aberration Inspector runs. In "
"the Focus **Options**, open the **Process** page, click the edit button next "
"to **SEP Profile**, copy the default profile under a new name (for example "
"``aberration``), and change these values:"
msgstr ""

